;; Lazy imports (PEP 810, Python 3.15; queue 239, doc/python/PY315-SURVEY.md P4b): CPython 3.15.2's
;; Objects/lazyimportobject.c, the lazy half of Python/import.c (_PyImport_LazyImportModuleLevelObject, sys.lazy_modules,
;; the pending submodules), ceval.c's _PyEval_LazyImportName and its reification at the loads of a global or a name,
;; moduleobject.c's getattr, sysmodule.c's API and initconfig.c's -X lazy_imports. A lazy_import object is made only by
;; a lazy import (the compiler's IMPORT_NAME flag 1, or flag 0 under the mode "all", __lazy_modules__ or
;; __lazy_import__), which only 3.15 reads; under 3.14 none exists, and every load pays one type test.


